participating-org.narrative:
Education Advocacy Network was first established as a lose network of member organizations championing the cause for education advocacy campaigning and stakeholder sensitisation in 2019. Through its advocacy efforts with the Ministry of Education and Sports, Ministry of Gender, Labour and Social Development and Ministry of Local Government, it was prudent that the status of the network transforms from being a lose platform to a fully registered NGO. Based on the recommendations by member organisations including UWEZO Uganda, FAWE Uganda, Rafiki Milele, Youth Line Forum, Niyetu and the Parliamentary Forum on Youth among other individual and institutions as members, the network fully registered with the National Bureau for NGOs. It is now fully registered and spanning its fifth yearof continued education advocacy at all levels namely, local, national, sub-regional and regional levels.

The mission of Education Advocacy Network is “to promote effective and reflective education advocacy that positively influences education policy and practiceat all levels of the country’s education system.”

Institutional objectives: As documented in the Strategic Plan, there are four objectives:

1. Ensure timely, relevant and quality advocacy efforts in the education sector;
2. Promote effective coordination of advocacy efforts to support community engagement at all levels;
3. Promote a stakeholder friendly environment for meaningful participation and engagement in all education processes at all levels;
4. Promote the development of a well-informed and resourced cadre of education advocates at local and national level.
The organization was registered to operate national wide in all the districts of Uganda. The organization works in all geographic areas of the country for it is national in operation. The key thematic program focus areas include, Basic and secondary education, Education Policy Advocacy, Membership growth and strengthening, community engagement andadvocacy as well as research and documentation.

The organization is legally registered and recognised as a contributor to the Ministry of Education and Sports vision, mission, goal and objectives. As a membership organisation its trust and credibility is guaranteed by the ministry of education and sports through continuous engagements and invitations it gets to participate in a number of itsprograms and activities. The organisation has thematic members whose work is structured according to the structures of the Ministryof education and sports.
